{
  "_doc": "Tier-2 church on Church Lane (Pell's Crossing, lot 'church', front faces the lane). Massing (ADR-0021): the nave and chancel rise two storeys under an open timber roof with tall lancets, the choir loft is a gallery over the back of the nave, the belfry is a three-storey tower through the roof's front with the broach steeple on its flat top, and the lady chapel and vestry are lean-tos against the chancel. Route: front doors chained -> round through the graveyard to the kicked-in vestry door -> vestry (daybook, the sick on the floor) -> chancel and nave (the congregation sits on in the pews) -> narthex: the pantry stair barricaded from below -> ladder up the tower into the belfry (Joan the keener, the pantry key) -> choir loft -> drop through the rotten boards onto the sealed pantry stair -> down to the fellowship hall (ambush among the cots) -> unlock the food pantry (loot, Rosa) -> back up, unbolt the side door by the fresh graves. Broach steeple sits astride the ridge over the belfry. See docs/POI_AUTHORING.md.",
